{
  "id": "point-light-display",
  "term": "point-light display",
  "definition": "A point-light display is a simplified moving image made from a small set of light points placed on key parts of the face or body so that motion can be seen while detailed structure is reduced. In this context, it is used to study how dynamic movement cues alone support recognition, such as identifying facial emotions.",
